    54	
    55	**T3. The south arc (ch31 sc2).** File along the turf, clockwise from east to south: Lira (knife) first, Karis, Oryn, Cael, Brom last and nearest the lip. The pack drifts across the floor toward them. The pale one comes to the rim over Brom's head and drops at him: the rolled rim gives its hind feet nothing square to push from, so it comes over reaching down, with its weight on its forelegs, and Brom's haft takes it under the jaw and puts it on its side on the turf. It gets up, shakes, and walks back round. The dark-backed one does the same thing in the same place, and gets the same. Nothing has told it. Cael calls the weight from the read ("Now"); Brom: "They don't mind me." A man they cannot hear.
