   145	## Owner flags (for a ruling)
   146	
   147	1. **The crossbow.** The packet has "Brom's bolt through the eye at thirteen feet" at the floor, and the ledger's entry state says that Oryn hands the bow to Brom at the stone on the 96th. Closed chapter 30 leaves it lashed on the mule west of the stone and counts "a hedging bill and two knives" at the den. I kept the manuscript: Oryn names the bow at the far lip, Seln fetches it during the retreat round the floor, and Brom spans it by hand. It costs about 500 words and gives Seln his part in the Ring. If the plan's staging is preferred, chapter 30 needs one line at the stone and one in the den's count, and chapter 31 loses the fetch (31:45–63; 31:237–259).
   148	2. **Four markers** (above). I composed nothing in the gaps.
   149	3. **Why west.** The eastern line is nearer by twenty-six yards. Cael's reasons are on the page: it is the hounds' door, steep, untrodden and hip-high with a quarter of an hour of light; the west is a trodden lane; and the bow settles it.
   150	4. **Why the pack comes by the west** (new canon, first item). It rests on the closed finding (they hunt discharge) and on Oryn's two counts at the stone at noon, and is left as a thing "put by", not a finding. Cut 31:29's second sentence if the plan wants no cause suggested.
   151	5. **Seln sent away at the first sight.** He is about two hundred yards off, at the mule, when Lira's arm is taken, and his window says what that weighs.
   152	6. **Cael holds through Lira's arm.** His reason is tactical and is said: any of the three would bring eight animals onto four people inside the length of a cart; "It needed room." He is not sure that he is right. Lira's window says that she would have made the same ruling.
   153	7. **The deployment number.** The log counts **twelve** uses in the Ring (the three lanes singly) and writes *thirteen*. The noon tests are named as left out, in one sentence, and stay unexplained. If the owner would rather the log stop giving a number after the Ring, cut 33:223–227 and the last line of 35:59.
   154	8. **Cael's one sentence to Oryn at the stone** (33:41): that what went up the hill with a light was himself, on purpose. She has seen eight of the nine used; she has not seen Shadow and nothing says that she has. She asks only about his calf. I judged that silence there would have read as a lie to her.
   155	9. **Blade's bill falls on Lira's knife** (the edge turned). It "took a morning's whetting" is not on the page; the knife is simply dull on the 96th. Movement 7 may want it sharp.
   156	10. **Seln's window** runs 2,293 words (plan 2,000) and gives him three things of his own: that he minds being unmarked; that Cael's "Say yours." is the first time anyone has asked for his report; and that seeing his craft in another person was like a mason seeing a course laid as he would have laid it. He says none of it aloud.
   157	11. **"Circles" in the plural.** Seln's protected line has "the circles", so he is asked, and says that one sheet had two rounds and that he cannot place the second. Nothing locates another site.
   158	12. **Seln strikes Cael's second reason** ("I shall not be a reason… I should sooner be known to that woman…"). It is his decision, and it means that Movement 6's telling is not held back on his account; the sources are still to be named "by Path, not by person", as that packet has it.
   159	13. **Karis speaks one word on the 99th** ("Wrong."), with two others that day unreported. The ledger has her voice back by about the 110th; "rough first" is Oryn's.
   160	14. **The covenant and Book 6's rule.** The loft treats the leaf as the third written under the Book 6 rule (before, at full weight); Cael says that the first rule, not to make one come, is kept, since Oryn proposed the reading. The notice still reads *Acquisition: directed*, as Blade's did.
   161	15. **"Stopping would be the lie"** is given a plain reason: to shut the place and call that a conscience would keep the wanting and send back only the bill. The text says that he does not tell himself it is right.
   162	16. **The third first** is "already written, on a leaf, in a loft": that he chose it for her. It is not set in the row.
   163	17. **Oryn shows no cost** at the moment of acquisition beyond the stopped current and the question. Movement 6 owns what, if anything, it took.
   164	18. **Length:** the Ring is over its allowance (10,858); the movement is under its budget (35,792 of about 38,000).
   165	19. **"the Ring"** appears as a name only inside the covenant; elsewhere it is "the ring", "that floor" or "quiet ground".
   166	
   167	## State at movement end (for the ledger)
   168	
   169	**Calendar.** The morning of the **hundredth day past the Line**, in Thornwater's back room, in the twenty-first minute of the long reading. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("first snow", "the snow", "the harvest", "frost"). Days on the page: 96 (sunset to night), 97, 98, 99, 100. Weather: frost every night; a north wind on the Fallow; ice on Thornwater's trough.
   170	
   171	**Where everyone is.** Cael on the plank table with Oryn's hands on him, the door shut. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln in or about the loft over the barn, with all three boxes and the covenant leaf in Hesk's book. The mule in Thornwater's yard. Five of the hold's people waiting until after noon.
   172	
   173	**Cael.** Eighteen. **Ten confirmed fragments** from the twentieth minute: the tenth is Tide-adjacent, partial, Iron, self and contact, *Acquisition: directed. Engagement: clinical — non-hostile.* It has not been tried, and its cost has not begun. The uncounted anomaly is untouched and unmentioned in this movement. **Deployment since the Line: thirteen** (the ford; twelve in the Ring on the 96th), as his log has it; the noon tests of the 96th are noted in the log as left out. Shadow used **once**. Ribs whole, the tape off on the 99th. Calf closed. Left forearm bruised and working. He has told Oryn two things: that what she saw on the hill was his doing, and, in the last minute, "I need to tell you what I am." He has told nobody why anything answered him inside, and has not told Lira since when he knew. Three letters still unanswered.
   174	
   175	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left forearm bitten through on the 96th, mended at the line; slung, and under the order until first snow** (nothing held, struck or caught). **Right ankle over a third time, taped, not mended**; she walks on the whole sole. The new tibia was run on for twenty yards and held. She knows that he chose not to act on the floor and that he had known he could; she has said "Later." and is keeping it. Her long knife is blunt.
   176	
   177	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. Eight finger-pads cut on the string, mended on the 97th; **no string until the hundredth**. He shot twice and killed twice. He carried the middle box through the whole of the Ring. He has the bill; the bow is his to carry and Karis has had the sleeve.
   178	
   179	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **Nine points and eight joins for a count of six at the line on the 96th**; about a tenth left that night; nothing since. Throat mended on the 97th; hoarse single words by the 99th. Holds: eleven Ring sheets, dry, not yet looked at; the box unopened; the carter's map with three rings (two still *guess*) and Seln's charcoal sheet; her leaf *Where / Entered as said / Blank. Stamped. Filed.*; the stub and the entry against herself of the 99th. The two torn leaves lay on the loft's boards. She has asked him nothing.
   180	
   181	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He fetched the bow, opened the jaws, carried Karis to the stone and called "Back". He has said "Compact" aloud once. He has given what he remembers of eight sheets and has refused to guess the file. He has released Cael from keeping the seal as a reason against telling Oryn. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
   182	
   183	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. Three mendings on the crew in two days; none since. She has crossed the line eight times alone at dawn on the 98th, which only Cael saw. She has read him five times at the surface and once at depth, and has found movement, "more than one", and no banks. She felt something change in him in the twentieth minute; she has been told that he did it and that he must tell her what he is; **she does not know the mechanism**. Thornwater's bench is owed four days and is put off until after noon.
   184	
   185	**Objects and money.** Board purse unchanged: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and eight in hand.** The Fallow hundred lies in Pike's box; no instruments were found; the posting (five strokes) is in Hesk's book. The crossbow, with **five bolts**, is with the crew; its spanning hook is in the mule's near-side pannier. One bolt lies on the Ring's floor. Six blankets returned, one a hand narrow. The rope is still owed.
   186	
   187	**Hounds.** Nine came; two are dead (one on the floor, one drawn off a hundred yards south of the stone, outside the line); **seven went north and south along the line's outside** on the night of the 96th and were not seen, tracked or heard again.
   188	
   189	**Pike's book and the wall.** Unchanged: seven lines; tenth; Teague nine up. The Fallow line has not been said. The two HOLD slips are unresolved on the page.
   190	
   191	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five. Oryn knows that he can do, inside a line, what no Path can; she saw Wind, a light, and heard an edge ring; she did not see the Shadow use and cannot attribute his arrival at Karis. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln saw it. All six know that the registry's iron stands on the line, that maps were drawn with a blank there, and that the posting was a question which their coming out has answered. Nobody knows where the file is, what it says, or why. Nobody has said why the fragments answer inside.
   192	
   193	**Open threads.** The telling, on the table, owed that minute. What it cost her, if anything. A leaf in a loft to be fetched and read. *Later*, on Lira's side. Seven hounds. A report going west with six on it. An arm slung until the snow, and an ankle that nobody has mended. Eleven sheets not yet looked at. Two rings marked *guess*. The top gate of a round, eleven days north.

