    29	- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** arrives by carter: “Six went in. Six came out.” It lands against Cael's memory of Gault's last line, *The instruments will not see its like.* Gault's physical leaf remains in the west with the withdrawal file and is not among the party's papers. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D5, N5] Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
    30	- **The first self-reading** that night, alone, as she set it. Ten flows and no banks (a limit of the reading, written above everything else). Then **the place session nine logged**: not a current, not the tenth, not any of the nine; near the middle, where everything is nearer; the ten go *round* it. Three things he can count. It is **not named**: no "still place" yet. The inventory, and **the three words retired with the reason** (protected). "Hundred and two in hand; six to the hold for the room and the kid."
    31	- **The week of tables (days 103–109).** The ring laid flat (eleven sheets one numbered rubbing to each upright, each upright's height recorded [corrected at M4 close]); the tally of *kinds* she will not number from one site. **Five findings, each a scene:** (1) *the Quieting*: grammar for a process, not a place; (2) **identical failure** across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, no ranking, Bronze, Iron R4; Lira's clock in Lira's words), and the looms sentence, unfiled (protected); Seln's "Six… I'm counting it." and the struck six; (3) **the strata as a physical demonstration** (four chips oldest to the right; the knife marked and the floor didn't; no stroke, no join, no laid edge; weathering past the founding stone), with **[UNBOUND] once** (protected), then Brom's "Say it with less."; (4) **the stakes, once, in four sentences**; (5) **the observation entered and the interpretation stopped**: "It's a fear." / "Does it help?" / "It's just correct." Oryn works the hold in the yard (nine late here, eleven at the next) and looks at the table once.
    32	- **New, a learning arc: Lira and the bowman.** The bowman off the gate-walk (unnamed) teaches her to shoot braced one-armed, against a rail and a knee, with the steading's bow spanned for her because she cannot span one-armed and says so. Short sessions, his few words, her fierce economy. This plants the Hall (M8). Oryn's order is kept exactly: the left arm holds nothing.
    33	- **C2, staged:** Oryn decides to leave her mule with the crew. Three boxes and a girl with one arm need it more than a healer whose holds keep beasts. She will take the next hold's beast at Millrace. Her decision, said in her register.
    34	- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
    35	- **Oryn's window north (111–112):** the spare rope, the road bending, what she carries in her head. It ends before Millrace.
    36	
    37	## What must remain true / withheld
    38	
    39	- **The still place is not named here.** It is "a place that does not flow." The phrase arrives in M8.
    40	- **Karis's hypothesis is never stated**, in dialogue or in her window. **[UNBOUND] appears once**, aloud, as a limit.
    41	- The debt to Oryn (telling her the self-reading) is **owed**, with the day set by her. It is not paid in M6.
    42	- No reading of anyone but himself. The tenth is used on no one else.
    43	- Vastin: one window only, three sentences, no age. "Forty years" is his rounding.
    44	- Daeva and Reydan: one log line.
    45	- Cash: 102 after the birthday. Brom's string restriction expires on day 100. The crossbow is back on his belt.
    46	
    47	## What the author owns
    48	
    49	The sensation-language of listening, kept to sensation; Thornwater in the hard-cold days [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] (ice on the trough, the grain going up the ladder past where they sleep); the tables' daily rhythm; the bowman's manner and words; the birthday's warmth and humor; the shape of each finding scene; all the windows.
    50	
    51	## Where we leave pressure
    52	
    53	Dawn on the 111th: Oryn north on a route seventeen days late at Oxhollow, carrying a spare rope; the crew with her mule, three boxes and a hundred and two in hand. A rule on the page and a debt with a date. Ten fragments and one place that doesn't move. "Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." The completion report has been on a desk somewhere for eight days.

