    70	
    71	**T11. Shadow, once, ten strides.** The price, in one breath: a run gives the animal all the time it wants; Wind lands him locked for a count beside Karis with eight coming to the crack; the sealed thing is the only one made to take something *out* of the air. Who can see: Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, who all know what he is; the healer, who does not, has Brom and a box between her and him, her back to him, and her eyes on Karis; the pack is not a witness; nobody else is nearer than two days. He lifts it behind Brom (use 2), passes Brom's right shoulder and Lira's through the standing grass on the north side, and lets it go with his hands on the animal. Oryn sees him arrive, not come.
    72	
    73	**T12. The throw.** The read gives him where its weight is; he takes it by the scruff and the root of the tail and puts his back into it; the tape says *there* and he goes through it. It lets go of her to find its feet. It lands a yard into the grass on the south side and rolls up.
