    42	
    43	Behind him the slope fell away to the east, and the line on that side was nearer by twenty-six yards. It was also the hounds' own door. There were three runs across it and not a stride of it that any of the six had walked; the grass stood hip-high the whole way down, the ground was steep, and in a quarter of an hour it would be dark. If they came out alive on that side, they would be half a circle of open country from a mule. The west was a lane trodden flat by their own feet, with a stone at the end of it that five of them could find with their eyes shut.
