   115	She had woken at first light and eaten the sixth of a loaf that lay by her head, and slept again, on purpose, for two hours by the sun. Then she had got up and washed to the elbow from the skin, and taped Lira's foot without a word, with an anchor turn and two strips up the outside and the long one crossed in front. After that she had sat with her back against a pannier and her eyes on the top of the sky.
   116	
   117	"I'll do them when it's straight up," she said. "You've all told me that's the hour those things have never been seen about. If I'm to shout twice more I'll do it then."
   118	
   119	Cael watched it from the grass, with his leg out.
   120	
   121	She took Karis first. Two fingers went to the inside of a thin wrist, and the other hand lay along the front of the throat, lightly, where there was a bruise the shape of two fists. Her lips went to ten.
