   145	She sat back, and Cael saw what the pair of them had cost her. She had been grey when she woke, and she was grey again. A Tide on a road had two in her, and she had spent the whole of yesterday's on one arm.
   146	
   147	"Leg," she said.
   148	
   149	He had not expected it. He had thought that she would take her two hours first; but she was looking at the calf, where a strip of grey blanket had gone dark in the night, and she held out her hand for it as for a tool.
