   191	[[TIER-B: Oryn sitting against the stake on the 97th, summing her mendings, "Three in two days… That's a route." — coordinator to supply protected text]]
   192	
   193	Cael had sat down across from her, with his leg out. He waited to learn whether she had more.
   194	
   195	"The top gate of my round's eleven days north of here," said Oryn. "That's by the road, at her pace." She tipped her head toward the camp, and the mule. "I'm not telling you for thanks. I've watched you. You count everything that's put in front of you, and that's a figure nobody would have put there."
   196	
   197	He had been counting, since a far lip, what the day had cost. He had Lira's arm in it, and a throat, and eight fingers; he had his own leg, and a number in a book. He had not had this. A woman had added a stop to the only thing she owned, for two reasons of her own, and the stop had taken three mendings in two days from seven gates that had not been asked.
   198	
   199	"I'd not have had it," he said. "I have it now."
