   252	
   253	"Somebody has sewn the pocket back into the coat," she said.
   254	
   255	Oryn had two fingers on her wrist already, and two on her neck, and her lips moved to ten.
   256	
   257	"Three parts full. It'll be the whole by the end of the week." She let go. "You spent it to the last copper once. Don't do that again where I'm not."
   258	
   259	She turned to the first of her two, and the lamp shone on her hands, and after that there was nothing to see but a woman kneeling.
   260	
   261	Cael sat on in the loft door until the cold drove him in. Tomorrow there would be an east gate, and a road with a bend in it; and for the first time since he had crossed the Line, six people would go out by a gate together where there had always been five.

