150:**Per-movement secondary share:** M1 3,300 (10%) · M2 3,200 (9%) · M3 5,800 (15%) · M4 2,600 (7%) · M5 4,000 (11%) · M6 8,700 (24%) · M7 4,600 (12%) · M8 8,100 (21%). Book total ≈40,300 (13.4%). The book-level 87/13 is the target that binds. M6 and M8 run window-dense because Oryn is off the road in both, and the windows follow her.
156:Formula §5: the protagonist gets **≈135 growth beats** (4.5 per 10k; one about every 2,200 words), spread evenly with a slight middle bump. By movement: M1 14 · M2 15 · M3 17 · M4 18 · M5 19 · M6 18 · M7 17 · M8 17. By thirds that is ≈42 / 48 / 45. Supporting characters get many small beats each (0.1–0.7 per 10k = 3–21 over the book). No deuteragonist.
