174:## 7. Progression plan
176:**Vocabulary** (this series' own): fragment, notice, integration, acquisition (directed), engagement (clinical — non-hostile), Path, declaration, tier, rank, Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver/Gold, Arbiter, sigil, idle state, deployment, the hold, discharge, the reading (surface / deep), mending, reserve, the line, quiet ground → the Quieting, perimeter, radius, stake, the board, HOLD, outcome, the wall. The system's voices are the **log** (Cael's inventory), the **notice** (one only, the tenth), and **Pike's ledger lines**. Interface text appears only where the canon calls for it.
178:**Density targets** (≈58 per 10k overall, front-loaded about 1.7x): **first third ≈81 per 10k** (M1 ≈82, M2 ≈82, M3 ≈78); **middle third ≈48** (M4 ≈50, with the line's mechanics taught as trials; M5 ≈42, with the acquisition spike; M6 ≈40); **final third ≈46** (M7 ≈40, M8 ≈55 with the inventory and the map). After M4 the system surfaces only at genuine turns: the notice, the self-readings, the rim, the fixed point, the inventory.
180:**How the first third teaches hard without spending anything:** the log's inventory of nine, with each fragment's idle rent named (Shadow at dusk, Anchor wanting doorways, Storm heavy); the discipline of holding as a skill with failure modes; the board's arithmetic (outcome, not tier); the carters' "don't declare"; the ford's discharge finding; the shale-backs' flight; Oryn's Tide taught in full (contact only, the reserve, three mendings a day, cannot heal herself, "cannot mend what I can't read," two readings); tier talk at the plank (Pike's Copper Force, Teague's unreported Bronze, Lira's Iron R1, Brom's Copper forever). **Cael deploys nothing in M1–M3 except the single ford burst.** The log reads "Deployment since the Line: one" from day 53 to day 90, and the edition keeps that count.
184:| **The hold** (method; not a fragment) | M1 taught as a discipline and given failure modes (Shadow drifting at dusk, Anchor's wants); M2 inverted at the ford (bait with one, kill with everything that isn't one); M5 dropped all at once inside the Ring | A sequence of small refusals, "arriving faster than a person could name them" |
185:| **Observation on animals** (method) | M1 the stretch (five items); M2 the ford's first mover; M3 the herd (no first mover; flight); M5 inside the Ring the pack is careless, because no prey there has ever shouted | Finds seams; names nothing it cannot count |
186:| **Wind-adjacent** | M2 one burst, openly, at the ford (the landing lock with a dog in it); M4 a foot's worth of evasion, silent, twenty strides inside the line (private); M5 two full bursts inside the Ring; M7 on the Stair's rim | The fixed one-count landing lock; never spend a burst near an opponent whose single hit he cannot price |
187:| **Iron-adjacent read** | M1–M3 held, even on the stretch; M4 run privately across the line and on the floor ("no seam"); M5 under his soles the whole retreat; M8 under water at the Hall ("the read at its dearest") | About a pace and a half; mass and vector, never intent; cheap and quiet; costs attention under water. At Gold weight, choose air or body/ground; never both. A Storm lane uses the air read and suspends body/ground reading until relinquished. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B3] |
188:| **Shadow-adjacent** (sealed) | Drifts at dusk in M1–M4 and is held. **Used exactly twice:** M5 ten strides to reach Karis (the informed B6 circle only; Oryn cannot see or attribute the use) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B2]; M7 up the stair and across the bowl, unseen by the rim, never attributable | Costs from waking; the seal's whole logic is restated once (M2 log) and honored |
189:| **Anchor-adjacent** | Wants doorways and the stake (idle); M5 perception only (sees Karis's points before they light); M7 the course **unbound from inside**; M8 the trial point, then **one fixed point held on the Hall's floor** | A point fixed *against* a surface; holding it against a biting thing costs "the whole of the rest". Perception is sure at about ten feet, faint at twelve, absent at fourteen; do not infer unbinding reach from perception. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1] |
190:| **Compression-adjacent** | M5 a hound taken at contact in the second lock; M7 at contact on the rim; M8 the wyrm's first strike taken into a standing frame | Bill in the ribs (the Hall's, carried into the cold) |
191:| **Pressure, Ember, Blade, Storm** | M5 spent as noise in the run (Ember one point held out; Storm seeding the rut; Blade ringing with nothing to cut); M7 the Daeva suite on the rim (Wind, Storm, Compression, Ember) | Storm is the heaviest thing he owns and resettles round any new arrival (M6, heard for the first time) |
192:| **Tide-adjacent (NEW, the tenth)** | M5 day 100 the deep reading; **the notice** (verbatim, §10); M6 cost: three days of *listening*, not pulling (his own current at the edge of thought; the nine audible as flows); the idle state learned by the third night; **the first self-reading** (a place near the middle that does not flow; location only; not named); M7 ask refused at the lean-to, granted on the road; the first reading of another person (Oryn: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things); M8 the second and third self-readings; **"the still place"** (the phrase appears first here); told to Oryn with his hand on her wrist; **Teague not read** | Contact only; surface at a count of ten, deep only with the subject still, whole and willing; does nothing in a fight; *ask first, every time*; "Things you keep touching don't heal" |
