316:- Ch19: Brom: "Ridge," — Seln: "They can shoot the bowl," … "They can't shoot the stair." — Oryn: "I can see what's wrong. I can't feel it and I can't touch it. Tape it. Leave the bolt." … "the bolt's the plug" … "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." — Oryn: "Ask first," — Lira: "Later." / "Later." — Oryn at the stone: "There. Back," … "The clock started again." — "It held a stair. It's not going to hold anything else this season." — Seln: "No faces." — Teague: "You walked out of the Quiet declaring," / "Yes." … "Then you're not on the board anymore. You're something the board doesn't have a column for."
320:- Ch23: Karis: "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." — "That's a healer's sentence," Oryn said … "I know whose it is," — Brom, Lira, Oryn at the first halt: "Twice," / "Twice," / "And not three," — Oryn at the fork: "I'm three weeks late there…" … "I've been a stop on my own route for nine days. I'm going back to being the route." … "Find me at Thornwater," … "Bring the map," — Karis: "Half the bend is twice the round. Four hundred. Near enough. Twice the radius. The same shape, at twice the size, round a thing I can't see." — Seln: "That's not a survey. That's a cordon. They've been here more than once." — Lira: "Twice the size. Is it twice the *anything else*?" — Cael: "Not without her. Not without knowing what a circle twice the size does to the four of you. And not without the map finished." / "It's finished," Karis said. "It's a line." / "Then it's a line that points somewhere. We go home and find out where."
321:- Ch24: Pike: "Teague says you need a column I don't have. I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." — the carters: "Eleventh," / "Aye," — Teague: "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted," — Pike: "Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," / Brom: "Ours," — Lira: "She'll say when," / Brom: "After the thaw," — *The sites were on an alignment. Not random.* — Karis: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) — **Closing, exact:** "I have ten things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no file I can see — and five people, one of them on a route, who've walked into the quiet three times and come out." He turned it over once and let it stand. "And a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." / Lira, one-armed, feeding the fire: "Then we follow it." / Brom: "After the thaw." / Karis, writing: "Noted." / Down the fire, the man who used to file reports about him watched the snow on the ferry landing with evident professional approval and said nothing, which — from him — was home. / Nothing out here had read him. At three floors older than any registry, every Path in the party had stopped at a line and his had not; a fourth had been paced from outside and not crossed. Nobody alive — least of all him — knew why. Someone had made the pattern. That was as far as anyone could say. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] [OWNER-pending #49]
