/bin/zsh -lc "rg -n 'Deployment since|deployment since|thirteen|twelve|deployment|uses? in the Ring|full-suite' editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/{BOOK_MAP.md,STATE_LEDGER.md,packets/MOVEMENT-006.md,packets/MOVEMENT-007.md,packets/MOVEMENT-008.md} universe/{UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md,STATE_LEDGER.md}" in /Users/drive/fractured-path-monroe13
 succeeded in 0ms:
universe/STATE_LEDGER.md:190:**Trajectory check:** ten at nineteen. The bible's twenty-two by Book 10 leaves twelve across Books 8–9 (and the B10 skip) — the Book 8 architecture must plan an accelerated rate and say so.
universe/STATE_LEDGER.md:267:| 11 | **Iron-Wall-adjacent** (partial; Iron family; a plane held, not a body hardened) | **Vastin** | **B8 Ch12** — the cut in Treswick | Entered, not told (the debt to Vastin stands); engagement field defensive/rooted; deployment none |
universe/STATE_LEDGER.md:274:**Trajectory:** thirteen at nineteen; "three of them in one city and one bridge — rate's climbing" (the log, Ch19).
universe/UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:242:Under Treswick's registry, in the Deepstacks (the old quarry the walls were cut from; a single iron leaf on pins; Cleon's key), among a bundle Cleon pulled from the galleries thirty years ago: twelve horn-coloured point-written leaves older than the board. One passage, read aloud once by Karis: the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land; one who "made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling … and set the apparatus over all the land"; the name scraped to the fibre (four or five letters; the first stroke); "that the un-bound should not come again"; ~four hundred years by the leaf's head. **The Architect** is the record's TITLE for the maker (Karis: "a title, not a name; the name's gone"). A later chronicle leaf: "he did not die in the way of men, but went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" then a thumb's width of nothing — MARKED, not read (Book 11's plant). The leaf's "list of parts" names the mark at the kindling and the mark on a sheet in the same line ("A mark is a grade"). The leaf stays on Cleon's shelf; the crew carries copies with the gap drawn.
universe/UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:248:Impulse along the line of the practitioner's frame at contact, from the ground through the body out at the hand; needs a thing to push against; a body's length; nothing at a distance; the RECOIL comes back along the same line every time (Teague's wrist clicks; the elbow; the shoulder — a third use in a fortnight would splint the arm). Cael's thirteenth (Force-adjacent, partial, Bronze) came at the Span's barricade; first used on stone at the pass (the second stack), recoil into the ribs; never on a person.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and eighty-five yards. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:20:- **The seal:** Shadow-adjacent is sealed from any witness who could carry the seeing west, because a defector's tradecraft in Cael's hands would confirm the surveillance-era acquisition. It costs from waking and drifts at dusk. Cael leaves it sealed past the Line; deployment since the Line is none. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D1, D3; F-rerun F2.4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:112:**Do not add:** any new fight with stillhounds before the Ring, which would spend the Ring's surprise. Any Compact face, name, policy, directive or office scene beyond Vastin's window. Any new Shadow-adjacent use (it is used exactly twice: Ring, Stair). Any fragment use in M1–M3 beyond the ford's single burst (the log counts "Deployment since the Line: one" through day 90). Any Daeva or Reydan contact beyond one log line each. Any Ephram, Withrow, Rooke or Bracken scene (letters only). Any Coss, Havel or Ilsev. Any Teague-crew name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:145:| **Seln** | 7,600 (2.5%) | M1: 1,800 (days 10–40: walking every road out of Lowmarch, and later Thornwater, alone; the report nobody asks for) · M5: 2,000 (day 97, at the stone, then the stake: the maps with holes unlocking; ends as he asks for the carter's map) · M7: 2,200 (night of day 112: the second slip held against the first in his head; twelve years carrying the case; wanting a face) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B6, C2] · M8: 1,600 (days 124–128: the ledger in his coat on the road home; giving it to Karis) | His fifteen years; the maps he carried and their blanks; the registry's form-prose; the case's known contents (the machine's maintenance records, read in B6); his read of the trap; his anger | Where the Quieting file is or what it says ("I carried the maps. I never saw the file."); any face or name on the rim; the case opened; the index decoded; the stroke-and-bar decoded; any sentence of affection said aloud |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:176:**Vocabulary** (this series' own): fragment, notice, integration, acquisition (directed), engagement (clinical — non-hostile), Path, declaration, tier, rank, Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver/Gold, Arbiter, sigil, idle state, deployment, the hold, discharge, the reading (surface / deep), mending, reserve, the line, quiet ground → the Quieting, perimeter, radius, stake, the board, HOLD, outcome, the wall. The system's voices are the **log** (Cael's inventory), the **notice** (one only, the tenth), and **Pike's ledger lines**. Interface text appears only where the canon calls for it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:180:**How the first third teaches hard without spending anything:** the log's inventory of nine, with each fragment's idle rent named (Shadow at dusk, Anchor wanting doorways, Storm heavy); the discipline of holding as a skill with failure modes; the board's arithmetic (outcome, not tier); the carters' "don't declare"; the ford's discharge finding; the shale-backs' flight; Oryn's Tide taught in full (contact only, the reserve, three mendings a day, cannot heal herself, "cannot mend what I can't read," two readings); tier talk at the plank (Pike's Copper Force, Teague's unreported Bronze, Lira's Iron R1, Brom's Copper forever). **Cael deploys nothing in M1–M3 except the single ford burst.** The log reads "Deployment since the Line: one" from day 53 to day 90, and the edition keeps that count.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:189:| **Anchor-adjacent** | Wants doorways and the stake (idle); M5 perception only (sees Karis's points before they light); M7 the course **unbound from inside**; M8 the trial point, then **one fixed point held on the Hall's floor** | A point fixed *against* a surface; holding it against a biting thing costs "the whole of the rest". Perception is sure at about ten feet, faint at twelve, absent at fourteen; do not infer unbinding reach from perception. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:278:- Ch8, Part-1 summary (EXC-B7-001): *Twelve weeks. Seven contracts. Pike says there's ground out here where the Arbiter goes quiet, and nobody goes in twice. Karis has been waiting her whole life for a sentence like that. Seln says the contract was written by someone from inside. I say it pays. Two days east, through Thornwater, on the day the healer said. For twelve weeks nothing out here has read me. I'd like to see what a place that reads nothing does with that.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:289:- Ch18: *Hundred and thirteenth day, the fork above Millrace. Oryn came. On her terms. She'll turn north the day she has to and I won't ask her not to.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈35,400. **Seln cutaway ≈2,200** (night of day 112, after the council: the two slips laid side by side in his head; twelve years carrying the case for people he cannot see [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B6]; why he wants a face; he may not open the case or decode anything). **Teague cutaway ≈2,400** (days 113–115: at Millrace, the five not back; the walk south to look; the rim's ground read in lantern light, the crossbows, "declaring"; holding the rim at dawn without being asked; no crew names).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:79:| 7 | Storm-adjacent (Gold-equivalent) | Daeva (edition B5 ch56) | Integrated; stability flag cleared in edition B6 M1 | Short-range pressure-differential/corridor lane. At Gold weight the read is air or body, not both. Lane bills: ten / ten / twelve counts, clean at eleven / eleven / thirteen; untested past three. After-effect: everything answers a beat late — bill, not flag. Heaviest fragment; resettles round a new arrival. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A4, B3, C1] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:80:| 8 | Anchor-adjacent (Silver-equivalent) | unnamed Compact operative, “the hand with no face” (edition B6 ch31/ch33/ch38) | Integrated | Fixed points, lines and a cage; purposeful unbinding once; uncommanded twelve-second doorway hold once. Perception sure at about ten feet, faint at twelve, absent at fourteen. Idle state wants doorways. Reach, rate and price otherwise unknown. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A5, B1, C1] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:86:**Deployment since the Line at entry: none.** It stays *none* until the ford's single Wind burst (day 53). It stays *one* through day 90, apart from the two unwitnessed tests on day 96, which are not logged as deployment.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:182:- Cael: age; fragments (count, any change, deployment since the Line); injuries open; idle-state notes; the still place's status; money (earned / in hand).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:199:- **Deployment since the Line: none, through day 49** — the line counts CAEL'S fragments (said once in ch1). Companions' native Paths (Lira's involuntary burst, Brom's Iron Skin rising, Karis's point-lit fires) are not his deployments. Shadow's dusk drifts on days 5 and 24 are entered as "rent", not use. Anchor's one uncommanded doorway hold is Book 6 history, recalled once at Thornwater's ladder; Anchor remains undeployed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:211:- **The plank (flag):** twelve feet of tarred ship's oak on two posts under the lower inn's eave; slips on bark, hide, a shingle or paper, each on one tack, with a small picture beside the words for people without letters; Pike's horn ink-pot set in a bored hole; his flat river stone for the page; an iron box bolted under the plank for the hirers' coin.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:223:- **The wash (flag):** three hours out on the east road; twelve feet deep and thirty across; a ramp on each side; a thorn stump on the eastern lip.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:232:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: the gate-to-stone distance is a hundred and ten YARDS (Cael paced it at a yard to the stride; Seln's hundred and four longer paces agree with it); the animal "tracked the buckle" and no sense is named anywhere; Pike's Thornwater line is printed once, in chapter 6, and its saying in chapter 7 is narration; the twelve-second doorway hold is recalled at Thornwater's ladder, not in the day-18 inventory. Word counts, metrics and line numbers elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:238:**Cael.** Eighteen, said to Pike on day 9. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly** (*Still open. Still real. Patience.*, written on day 18). **Deployment since the Line: none.** No injury; the forearm is "sound again" by day 5 and is not mentioned afterward. Idle states: Shadow sealed, costing from waking, drifting at dusk (two drifts, logged as rent); Anchor asking at every sill, gate, rim and rail; Blade asking *Edge?* and taking names; Storm heavy; Wind leaning his feet. He has not read the Iron read once. The log has an entry for most days, each ending on the deployment line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:250:**Pike's book and the wall.** A heading of five names; **four lines**: *Ferry, the landing's goods. Six crossings stood. Nothing lost. Two marks.* (day 14); the fence (forty posts cut and set; four marks and flour; the saying is not on the page); the wash (three marks; not on the page); and the protected Thornwater line (day 49). **Thirteenth of thirteen; eleven lines between theirs and the top.** The top line is *Teague.* On the plank: *Thornwater ford. Clearance. Forty marks.* with *HOLD. Teague.* in Pike's capitals.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:260:- **The companions have failed before succeeding at the hold:** Lira has one involuntary practice burst, Brom has let Iron Skin rise and put it down, and Karis has lit at ninety and later held unlit to three hundred. These are native-Path events, not additions to Cael's deployment count (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:21-65`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:7`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:266:- **Board texture at handoff:** four earned lines, thirteenth of thirteen with eleven between them and Teague, Thornwater's ford held under Teague's name, and Pike's plank physically crowded but not count-fixed (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:103-123,181-227,271-277`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:277:- **Deployment since the Line: ONE** — a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53. None before; none after. Shadow is unused by Cael and stays sealed. Seln's use of his OWN native Shadow Path under water at the ford is not Cael's deployment and stands (it tested the water clause).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:287:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial (pass; one register priority), cold read (three clarity items), source-distance (6 tracked passages, no dense scene), plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — twelve applied by the coordinator). Same-author repair r1 in progress when this block was written; the CLOSED note follows below when the recheck returns.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:305:- **Lowmarch:** undirected eastbound mail stops at Pike's plank; he gives out each piece twice and reads letters at dusk to people who have no letters; a spike under the plank holds finished slips; he rewrites the whole wall on fresh sized sailcloth when the order changes; a crew entered as *the shingle pair* is thirteenth from day 60.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:315:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53, in front of the hold's bowman). Shadow unused; it lifted at dusk through the wait at the ford and again on the walk down the bar and was refused. Ember offered a point in the hound's mouth over Karis and was refused. The Iron read stays shut. Left calf bitten through on day 53: a leg on level ground, nine strides uphill. He has not asked Seln for his report, has not answered Lira's question, has not answered Hesk's letter, and has stopped counting Lira's runs. He knows that he had a grandmother who crossed the Line once on a trade run; no name, no line of descent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:327:**Pike's book and the wall.** **Six lines** under the five names: the protected ford line (said on day 60) and *The well at the south fork. Air cleared, shaft drawn, six stones set. Four marks.* (day 64). **Twelfth of thirteen; Teague eleven up.** The ford slip is with the finished slips, struck with one line through Teague's name and five strokes beneath, and Thornwater's mark at the foot. Fourteen slips on the plank on day 60; a bare tack set by the left-hand post on the evening of day 69 for a hold's slip expected from the north-west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:334:Movement 3 already carries the day-70 injury snapshot, fifty-two in hand, Teague out on two holds, the unmended ankle, and deployment count one (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:16-18,35-42`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:341:- Board/account state beyond the packet's purse figure: six earned lines, 62 earned total, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up; Pike has set a bare tack for the incoming unnamed ford slip (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-465`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:345:**Movement 2 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the twelve audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Lira herself says "There isn't one." at the gate; her later question follows from her own inference); six tracked passages recomposed; hound identifiers and count anchors at the ch10–ch11 handoff; nine recap restatements removed; a recovery bridge before Lira's run. Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE**, no line fixes; all six tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 15 protected. 37052 words. Facts changed by the repair (wording only): Seln sees Cael's calf wound first; Cael is already writing when Karis corrects his verb and dictates the finding; Hesk's letter is known by its fold.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:351:- **Deployment since the Line stays ONE.** No fragment was used on the mountain: Compression and Anchor wanted, and Cael held. Shadow sealed and unused. Lira's burst on day 78 is her own native Wind; her body went about twenty feet and her DECLARATION, with its crack, crossed the gorge.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:395:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:411:**Pike's book and the wall.** Unchanged since the 69th: six lines, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up. The traverse is not yet said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:424:- Cael's three left-low ribs were broken day 78 and received five bands on day 81, to be lifted on day 99 by Oryn if possible; his reopened calf is only cloth-bound. His nine fragments are held, Shadow remains sealed, and deployment since the Line is one (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-155`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-45`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-333`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:429:- Pike's board has not yet heard the traverse: six lines, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up remain the last spoken standings until the marked slip reaches Lowmarch (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-465`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:174-176`). Hesk's letter is still unanswered, Lira's earlier question remains unanswered, and two stillhounds remain open downstream (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-451`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:329-331`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:438:- **Cael's two private tests** (day 96, a quarter of an hour, a cord north of the stone, unwitnessed) are NOT deployments and are not logged as such. Deployment since the Line stays ONE. Shadow untouched. He has told nobody; his reasons are on the page and he distrusts them. The day-96 log omits the deployment line for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:485:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** Logged deployment since the Line: one (the ford); the day-96 entry carries no deployment line. **On the 96th, unwitnessed:** the Iron read opened a pace short of the line and carried across it; a foot's worth of Wind evasion twenty strides inside; the Iron read once more on the floor. Shadow is sealed and untouched; it lifted at dusk on the 95th at the turn of the ruts and on the 96th inside the line, and was refused both times. Anchor asked at the stone and at the stake. Ribs: taped, eighteen days from the break, three to go. Calf: bound in Oryn's linen, closing by itself. He has told nobody that anything answered him inside, and has given Karis "It was dark before… It's dark now." for her sixth row. Hesk's satchel holds the log, the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter, Pike's lines on bark, and now Ephram's letter and Vell's. He has not answered any of the three.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:514:- **Secret/action count:** Cael alone knows the Iron read, foot of Wind and floor read worked. Shadow is unused; deployment since the Line remains one, and the day-96 log deliberately has no deployment line (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:239-299`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:63-77,219-235`).

