   155	They walked west on the ninety-eighth, and Lira went the whole way on the flat of her foot, since she had been told to.
   156	
   157	"Whole sole," the healer had said, at the stone, with the tape freshly on. "Heel and toe together, every step. You don't roll off it and you don't push. If it goes a fourth time, I'm not carrying you to that fence."
   158	
   159	"I could ride."
