editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-37.md:131:"I can feel that there's movement. More than one. I can't count them — I can't find where one stops. There's no channel. Everyone has a channel; I feel the banks and I know the Path. I can't find the banks in you. I've looked for twenty minutes. It isn't that you're broken. It's that I can't find anything shaped like the thing I read."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-37.md:135:*More than one.* She had it. She did not know what she had. She had gone through a house with a lamp and counted more rooms than a house ought to hold, and she had stood in every one of them and could not find a wall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-35.md:13:"You'd be shutting eight new fingers on a hind leg. Stand there."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-36.md:91:"I shall not be a reason. You shut that thing for my sake, and you have kept it shut at a cost that I watched you pay in a river. But I have had four nights in which to consider who was looking in a lane, and I find that I should sooner be known to that woman than be used to keep her ignorant of a thing that is to be done to her. Strike the second. It is not available to you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-36.md:121:He had not shifted from his place on the boards. He was looking at his own open hands, where a healer had drawn eight new lines.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-36.md:207:*The conditions, as I have them. Sustained: twenty minutes at contact is longer than any bout I've stood. Stakes: I'm three days off the Ring and the nine are still settling; she's three mendings down and her route's late at the far end and she's spending a fourth on a patient who's given her nothing four times. Earnest: she'll do the thing she does as well as she does it. Karis: the model says real, not fight. I don't know if the model's right. Nobody does. Tomorrow's the first time it could be tested and I'm the test.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-34.md:99:He did not have the leaf. There would be one. A sheet with a hole in it has a page somewhere that says what the hole is for; that was how every office that he had ever served drew breath. He had never seen it. He did not know what room it lay in, or under what heading, or whose hand had ruled those rounds. He knew the weight of a tin and the number of its sheets, and he knew that he would be asked for more than that before the sun was high, by a small person with a pencil and no voice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-34.md:197:He had been counting, since a far lip, what the day had cost. He had Lira's arm in it, and a throat, and eight fingers; he had his own leg, and a number in a book. He had not had this. A woman had added a stop to the only thing she owned, for two reasons of her own, and the stop had taken three mendings in two days from seven gates that had not been asked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-34.md:243:"The Compact knows what quiet ground does."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-33.md:27:Brom had the bow between his knees already. He set his boot in the stirrup a third time, with eight fingers that he had not yet let anybody see, and drew, and Cael heard his breath go in through his teeth. He laid a bolt on it, which left three in the sleeve. Then he walked ten yards to the north and stood there with his back to the lantern, a broad dark shape with a box still on it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-33.md:171:Across the pads of four fingers on each there was a cut, straight, as though it had been ruled, and in two of them it had gone deep. They had bled down into his cuffs and dried. He had drawn that string three times with them, the last time when they were already open, and he had stood an hour in the frost with the stock in them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-33.md:197:*Lira: left forearm bitten through and held; mended at the line, an hour, by lantern. One arm till first snow, by order. Right ankle gone a third time, and not mended. Karis: throat; no voice. Brom: eight fingers, on a string. Seln: nothing. Oryn: spent to the bottom, and asleep on the road.*
