+   new: `"Everyone I've ever had my hands in, this is the part where I know." She said it as a finding about herself. "Iron Skin, you feel the banks first — dense, walled, everything held. Ember, the banks are a fire's, hot at the edge. Wind you barely feel the banks at all, the water's too fast. But there's always a bank. It's how you know which river." A pause, long, her current going along Ember and stopping at the ignition point and lying there as if it had found a stone in a bed. "I can't find one here. I keep putting my hand where the bank ought to be and there's more water."`

