10:'The hand was the pads of four fingers laid open by a string in the dark, bled into the linen and dried there, and she soaked the linen off with the pan\\'s water and a corner of the lantern\\'s oil, slowly, while Brom looked at the scrub. When it was off she turned the hand over in the light and said, \"String,\" as a verdict, and put her palms round it.\\n\\nShorter than the throat; less than half, by the floor. The fingers, when she opened her hands, had four dark lines across the pads where there had been four open mouths, and Brom closed the hand and opened it.\\n\\n\"Nothing on the string for three days,\" Oryn said. \"Span it with the stirrup and your foot, like a man who\\'s had his fingers opened once, which you are now. You\\'ll not lose the lines. That\\'s two.\"',
12:'\"Three in two days,\" Oryn said, after a while, to the country.\\n\\nHe waited.\\n\\n\"The arm. That was last night, and it was one, and it was the size of two. The throat. The hand. Three mendings in two days.\" She turned her hands over on her knees and looked at them, and let them lie. \"That\\'s a route. Near enough, that\\'s what I carry between a hold and the next one, for the people who feed me and shoe the mule. Three serious hurts and a road\\'s worth of small ones. And I\\'ve spent it on a road two days from the nearest roof, on a crew that\\'s not on my circuit, sitting against a piece of iron somebody drove where they\\'d measured to.\"',
21:'\"Everyone I\\'ve ever had my hands in, this is the part where I know.\" She said it as a finding about herself. \"Iron Skin, you feel the banks first — dense, walled, everything held. Ember, the banks are a fire\\'s, hot at the edge. Wind you barely feel the banks at all, the water\\'s too fast. But there\\'s always a bank. It\\'s how you know which river.\" A pause, long, her current going along Ember and stopping at the ignition point and lying there as if it had found a stone in a bed. \"I can\\'t find one here. I keep putting my hand where the bank ought to be and there\\'s more water.\"'}
