+# RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — protected-text restoration and four narrow canon repairs
+
+The movement may be ratified after the exact fixes below. The Ring, calendar, deployment arithmetic, tenth-fragment acquisition, and all required turns are structurally sound. Required repair is limited to: (a) restoring the four Tier-B units; (b) reconciling Brom's injury to the protected source's one hand/four finger-pads; (c) removing two unprotected claims about what the unknown file contains; and (d) keeping Seln's identity sealed when he strikes Cael's second reason. No scene rebuild is required.
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+- **Entry state — PASS.** Chapter 31 opens at the den under the eastern lip with the floor between the six and the western stone (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:3-11`), exactly where closed chapter 30 leaves them, with the mule and covered crossbow west of the stone (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:3-9,219-239`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:480-485`). The eleven finished rubbings remain on Brom's back (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:65-73`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:99,131-163,237`).
+- **Crossbow — KEEP; no retroactive change to chapter 30.** Closed chapter 30 leaves the covered bow lashed to the mule (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:3-7`). Oryn names it and its six-bolt sleeve from the far lip (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:45-51`), Seln fetches it on the declared three-hundred count (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:55-63,237-251`), and Brom spans it by stirrup and hand (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:253-265`). That is the closed-text solution to packet shorthand, not a contradiction. The accounting is six: floor shot, stone shot, three left in the sleeve and one loaded at the night watch (`manuscript/chapter-32.md:3-9`; `manuscript/chapter-33.md:27-37`); the stone bolt is recovered, yielding five carried from the 97th (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:15-21,53`). Brom draws no string after the 96th, and the prohibition expires on day 100 (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:139-143`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:45`).
+- **Ring geometry — PASS.** The manuscript preserves the eastern den, 26-yard-stride floor, 207 yards from western lip to stone and 233 yards from den to western line (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:5-11`), against the closed 220 yards from floor centre to stone and the eastern den (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:21,43-45,61,165-189,215`). The natural north-west rain-rut is not a made feature (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:11`); the pack returns from the west by the party's lane (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:19-29`); the bands remain round the feet of all eleven uprights, not the lip (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:43-47`). No cord length or Karis stride length is stated.
+- **Bodies — PASS except Brom's protected-text contradiction.** Lira's ankle goes a third time and her new tibia is run on for twenty yards (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:165-193`); the left forearm is taken, held rather than shaken, mended, slung, and ordered unused (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:189-235,289-315`; `manuscript/chapter-33.md:85-125`). Cael's calf opens in the rut, his left forearm takes the Compression-first-beat bill, his ribs remain taped through day 99, and all three states close on schedule (`manuscript/chapter-32.md:201-219,239-255`; `manuscript/chapter-35.md:265-329`). Karis's throat course is consistent from loss of voice through rough single words (`manuscript/chapter-32.md:85-135`; `manuscript/chapter-34.md:125-131`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:9`). **Contradiction:** the protected source makes Brom's injury one hand, four finger-pads, four open mouths (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-12.md:67-73`), while the draft repeatedly makes it both hands/eight pads (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:27,167-179,197`; `manuscript/chapter-34.md:133-143,197`; `manuscript/chapter-35.md:13`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:9,121`). Fixes 2–7, 9–11, 14, 16–17 and 19 restore the governing protected fact throughout.
+- **Objects, money, letters, and obligations — PASS.** The board account remains 132 earned/108 in hand and the rope remains owed in kind (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:19,113,247-251`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:499-503`); the Fallow hundred is not paid because no instruments are found (`manuscript/chapter-32.md:309`; `manuscript/chapter-34.md:273-289`); three letters remain unanswered and the two HOLD slips remain open (`STATE_LEDGER.md:499-505`). The eleven Ring sheets, two other boxes, case, maps, posting, mule, blankets and recovered bolt all survive in their governed locations (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:33-37`; `manuscript/chapter-34.md:259-273`; `manuscript/chapter-35.md:15-21,283-301`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:480-505`).
+- **Knowledge — PASS after fixes 8, 15 and 18.** The five mechanism-knowers remain the only witnesses to Shadow; Oryn sees the hill's results but not the discontinuity and still lacks the mechanism at the close (`manuscript/chapter-32.md:97-125`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:216-244`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:191`). The draft's unprotected assertion that a hidden page says what the hole is for (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:99`) and its later assertion that such a page exists in a room (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:267`) spend withheld file content against `MOVEMENT-005.md:54`; fixes 8 and 15 remove both. Seln may release Cael from using him as a reason, but may not offer his identity: Movement 6 requires sources named by Path, not person (`MOVEMENT-006.md:26`), so fix 18 amends `manuscript/chapter-36.md:91`.
+
+## 2. Movement plan and owner flags
+
+### Beat/order audit
+
+- **Ring retreat — PRESENT and ordered.** Nine appear; west is chosen; Seln fetches the bow; Brom holds the lip; Lira's ankle and arm fail; the retreat counts down; Karis falls at sixty; Shadow covers ten strides; Cael stops holding and runs the full suite; the rut sends him east before he returns west; Compression takes the second lock; Brom shoots at six feet; Karis's nine points light; seven leave north/south (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:17-63,145-317`; `manuscript/chapter-32.md:1-309`). This follows `MOVEMENT-005.md:43`.
+- **Shadow staging — PASS strictly.** Cael is ten strides from Karis; Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln have the sightline; Brom and the box screen Oryn, whose attention is on the bodies; Oryn does not turn during the transit; Cael releases at ten (`manuscript/chapter-32.md:97-125`). Oryn can see where he arrives without seeing him come, so she cannot attribute the use; the pack is never treated as a witness (`manuscript/chapter-32.md:113-125`; `manuscript/chapter-33.md:203-205`).
+- **Inside the line — PASS.** Lira has no Wind, Brom no Skin, Karis no Ember, Seln no Shadow and Oryn no Tide inside (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:165-175,201-235`; `manuscript/chapter-32.md:85-135`). Karis's nine points are deliberately set on the last outside handbreadth where a point holds; Cael crosses the stone before she lights them, and she is kneeling a stride west/outside (`manuscript/chapter-32.md:273-295`). Thus no companion uses a Path inside.
+- **Camp, return, council, reading — PRESENT and ordered.** Lantern mending/order/log/close occupy chapter 33 (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:39-277`); morning arithmetic, route, Seln's map memory and posting reread occupy chapter 34 (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:1-307`); the 98th–99th return, Oryn's eight private crossings, Thornwater examination and reading terms occupy chapter 35 (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:63-367`); the loft council and covenant precede the reading (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:1-227`); the twenty-minute reading, acquisition, exact notice and final debt follow (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:229-275`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:1-244`). This matches `MOVEMENT-005.md:44-48`.
+- **Withheld items — PASS after fixes.** No one theorizes why the fragments answer; “Quieting” does not occur; “Compact” is spoken once by Seln (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:243`); the hounds' later direction remains unobserved (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:193-195`); Oryn ends without the mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:216-244`); and no integration cost is paid or Tide use attempted (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:188-202`). The file and Seln-identity exceptions are the repairs above.
+
+### All 19 AUTHOR-REPORT owner flags
+
+1. **KEEP — crossbow.** Closed chapter 30 governs; the six-bolt and retrieval continuity is exact (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:3-7`; `manuscript/chapter-31.md:45-63,237-265`).
+2. **REPLACE — four Tier-B markers.** Fixes 1, 10, 12 and 21 restore the full source units (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:293`; `manuscript/chapter-34.md:135,191`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:67`).
+3. **KEEP — west.** The east is 26 yards nearer but steep, untrodden, darkening and the hounds' door; west is the known lane and the bow is there (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:41-55`).
